/*1...> Marker interface in an interface which doesn't have any methods and fields
    and it act like signe to JVM or compiler to provide the specific behaviour to the objects at rin time
    ex: 1.> Serializable
    2.> Cloneable
    3.> RandomAccess
    4.> Remote
    5.>ThreadSafe

    How JVM identify MarkerInterface
    1.> JVM checks if the object implements the Marker Interface
    2.> If yes, provide the special behaviour
    3.> else throw exception

    When to use Marker Interface
    1.> when u to want provide special behavior without adding any method

    difference between Abstract class and marker interface

    Abstract class                                   marker interface
    1.> it can have methods                        1.> no methods
    2.> used for abstraction                       2.> used for tagging
    3.> zero overhead                              3.> Slight overhead due to method implementation

